#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124205 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "ccfdc303-534f-530e-810b-f475a997f5d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4703" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072258/assets/bc54c8852a673014f5bb9c7f3b7c07b5f2414d8edf0cea79e2b410211e97ae20.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072258/assets/c31f9eb258350b5f9cc63d2e96a3e68122428b64e097451d7b9a12a3b58750c3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124206 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "22a77802-4114-516f-a0e0-4cda2e069361" :question/math-academy-id "e-4704" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072258/assets/bbc4e9e0d0497930f434cd3dade35973105401ba72c74690d924c6390d87413d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072258/assets/da73e68fe8bc5e6baa8876beb17d702707cb0ad43831f42ecfa45f3a98d43202.png)\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124207 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6e4b2e85-86a8-5050-a60a-ae8d40453ad0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4705" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072258/assets/eb0fc447f75650bb47da114b8cd4f0986b5f501333f61005e2c1f4989c3a11ed.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124208 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "3ac076bd-5add-5c08-bb96-7b11c0a37d54" :question/math-academy-id "e-4706" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072258/assets/b57dc02f6baddfcb517ccf12366320534074b33814577b4a2d1010377325fc19.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{2}{7}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcb2620f-3703-5699-8753-08eb0f45687b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375599} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa7f5d1-7387-5a44-b1b8-0fb3f267a423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375600} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2865da-de90-58e8-9278-5a920f30c1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375601} {:answer/id #uuid "4da345a9-e107-50fc-bdc9-4e5e09dea646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375602} {:answer/id #uuid "4a938d0d-eb8b-5127-9b9c-2ca2563fd838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All the columns are pivot" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e2865da-de90-58e8-9278-5a920f30c1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375601} :answer-field/id #uuid "73ce5cbf-cca4-5edf-87ce-2867ed82e8d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0565b425-ebb4-5d4a-bad6-acea463e950b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130930" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\be